  "sale_events": [],
  "body": "Life feels wonderfully open here, where peaceful natural bush views and an extraordinary 9,039sqm landholding create a rare sense of space and privacy. Built just a few years ago by the current owners for their own family, this approx. 657sqm residence occupies only a small portion of the site, leaving an impressive expanse of flat open land.\r\n\r\nFor golf enthusiasts, imagine your own putting green or par-3 practice range, perhaps complemented by a pickleball court or private recreation area. The scale of the land may also offer future potential to explore, subject to relevant council requirements and approvals.\r\n\r\nInside, the home has been thoughtfully designed for modern, multi-generational living, with a practical layout offering both shared and private spaces.\r\n\r\nFour generous living areas cater to entertaining, everyday family living and private retreat. The flexible studio includes its own bathroom, offering a private space for grandparents or teens, a home office or quiet retreat.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home, East meets West with two dedicated kitchens, a Western style kitchen and a separate Asian style kitchen, supporting both everyday cooking and entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe home features five bathrooms, including four ensuites, with two master suites each enjoying their own private living area. The main master suite also includes a walk-in wardrobe. One separate toilet, a versatile additional room suitable for a gym or other uses, and three-car internal garaging complete the layout.\r\n\r\nAlbany Mega Centre and Westfield Albany are around eight minutes away, while Long Bay Town Centre and Regional Park are approx. a 10-minute walk. Pinehurst, Kristin and Massey University are also around 10 minutes by car, with zoning for Long Bay School and Long Bay College, plus easy motorway access to Auckland's CBD.\r\n\r\nThis exceptional home combines striking architecture, substantial flat land, peaceful natural surroundings and a highly convenient Long Bay location.\r\n\r\nSpace to breathe, room to dream and views that never get old.",
